---
import Base from '../../../layouts/Base.astro';
import NnMasthead from '../../../components/NnMasthead.astro';
import race from '../../../content/race.json';

// The same event theme as every other page under /nn/ — see packages/shared/styles/nn-theme.css.
//
// **The horror stops at the edge of the card**, exactly as it does on the privacy notice and
// the course page. The hero is the campaign's; the document itself is ink on white, because
// this is the page somebody reads before agreeing to be bound by it.
import '@src/shared/styles/nn-theme.css';

// **This page is the race director's copy, transcribed verbatim, and it is not ours to edit.**
//
// Kayleigh supplied the entry terms and race rules on 28 August 2026 and they are published
// here word for word — her capitalisation, her punctuation, her "will"/"shall", her ordinals.
// Where the words read oddly they are still hers: this is the document a runner agrees to be
// bound by when they tick the box on `/nn/2026/`, so a tidy-up here is a silent change to a
// legal instrument. Suggested corrections go to her as a batch and come back as new copy with
// a new version line at the foot of this page. **Do not edit this text for style.**
//
// The one exception is the ARC permit number, which is rendered from `race.json` rather than
// from the supplied copy — see the note at the bullet itself.
//
// ## Facts come from `race.json`; only the prose is here
//
// Every fact on this page that also appears somewhere else on the site is interpolated from
// the race-facts file: the date, the short date, the permit, race HQ's name, the transfer
// deadline, the number-collection time and the contact address. A fact that drifts between
// the entry page and this one is the failure this rule exists to prevent, and it is a worse
// failure here than anywhere else — the entry page and the terms page disagreeing about a
// deadline is a dispute with a runner who has paid.
//
// **The contact address appears twice and is one value.** Two literals that could diverge is
// precisely what is being avoided; both bullets read `race.contact`.
//
// **`hqName` and `dateShort` are narrow forms of facts this file already states in full**, and
// they exist because the supplied sentences use the short form: "the Race HQ at Ashton Park
// School", not the full postal address, and "on 1 November", not "on Sunday 1 November 2026".
// Deriving either by splitting the long form — an address on its first comma, a date on its
// weekday — is a templating scheme cleverer than the one in use here and it is fragile in a
// way nothing would catch. Two adjacent keys in one file are honest about the cost instead.
//
// ## The clock is not converted, deliberately
//
// **Every time on this page is a pre-formatted civil-time string, interpolated raw**, which is
// the same treatment `entriesOpen` and `entriesClose` get on `/nn/2026/`. It is not an
// oversight and it is not a route around the London-time helpers: turning "3pm on 16th
// October" into an instant means *choosing an offset*, and the choice is the bug — the
// transfer deadline falls in BST and the race falls in GMT, eight days after the clocks go
// back. `packages/shared/src/entry-state.ts` states the same rule for the same reason. There
// is nothing here to convert because nothing here is an instant.
//
// See docs/architecture/principles.md#stop-and-ask
const canonical = 'https://new.southvillerunningclub.co.uk/nn/2026/terms/';

// **The number-collection time is the schedule's, not a second copy of it.**
//
// `09:15` is stated once in this repository — the registration row of `race.json`'s schedule,
// which `/nn/2026/race-day/` renders as the morning's running order. This page asks that row
// for it by name rather than by position, because the schedule has been reordered once
// already and an index would have gone quietly wrong; and by `id` rather than by matching the
// prose, because a copy edit to "Collect your number" would otherwise break this page with
// nothing to say why.
const registration = race.schedule.find((row) => row.id === 'registration');

// **A missing row fails the build rather than rendering a hole.** `registration?.time` would
// print "from  onwards on 1 November" — a sentence with a gap in it, on a legal document,
// with nothing failing anywhere. This runs at build time, so removing or renaming that row
// stops the deploy and says why.
if (registration === undefined) {
  throw new Error(
    "race.json has no schedule row with id 'registration', so the terms page cannot state " +
      'when race numbers are collected. Restore the row or update this page.',
  );
}
---

<Base
  title="Entry terms and race rules — Nightingale Nightmare 2026"
  description="The entry terms and conditions and race rules for the 2026 Nightingale Nightmare, as supplied by the race director."
  canonical={canonical}
  theme="nn"
>
  {
    /* The campaign navigation, as on every other page under /nn/. Somebody who opens the terms
    from the entry form to check the transfer deadline should not have to retrace their steps
    to carry on entering. */
  }
  <NnMasthead slot="masthead" />

  <header class="nn-hero nn-hero-compact">
    <div class="nn-wrap">
      <h1>Nightingale Nightmare Entry Terms and Conditions</h1>
    </div>
  </header>

  <div class="nn-wrap">
    <div class="nn-card nn-prose">
      {
        /* **Two sections, two real lists.** A legal document read on a phone is skimmed, and a
        `<ul>` is what lets somebody skim it — a screen reader says "list, thirteen items" and
        a sighted reader gets the same shape from the bullets. Paragraphs with dashes in front
        of them would give neither. */
      }
      <h2>Entry Terms and Conditions</h2>

      <ul>
        {
          /* **`{' '}` is a real space and a line break is not.** Prettier moves a bare
          `{expression}` onto its own line, and `compressHTML` collapses the newline either
          side of it rather than keeping it as a space — so this renders
          "held onSunday 1 November 2026" without the explicit space. The same trap is
          documented at the head of `nn/privacy.astro`, in `NnRaceSummary.astro` and in
          CLAUDE.md, and it has been hit in this repository three times. */
        }
        <li>
          By completing this registration process you acknowledge that you are entering
          the Nightingale Nightmare, to be held on {race.date}.
        </li>
        <li>The event is organised by {race.privacy.controller}.</li>
        {
          /* **The permit number is the repository's, not the supplied copy's.** The copy reads
          "ARC/26/ 0842" with an internal space; the number issued on 27 August 2026 is
          `ARC/26/0842`, and it is stated once in `race.json` and quoted on `/nn/2026/` and at
          the foot of the entry form because ARC require it on entry forms and advertising
          material. Rendering the space here would mean changing `race.json`, which would move
          the number on both of those surfaces and fail `site.spec.ts`. Confirmed with the race
          director as a transcription slip, and it is the one character on this page that is
          not hers.

          **`<strong>` because this is a number somebody skims for**, along with the transfer
          deadline below. It is emphasis on a fact, not a change to the words. */
        }
        <li>
          This race is run under an ARC permit and under ARC's rules of competition.
          Permit number <strong>{race.permit}</strong>
        </li>
        <li>
          You confirm that the email address and personal details you provide to us are
          all accurate, correct and up to date.
        </li>
        <li>
          Participation in/attendance at the Event is personal to you and you thereby
          declare yourself medically fit to participate.
        </li>
        {
          /* **Both contact bullets read the same value.** `race.contact` is the address the
          entry form, the sold-out notice, the guide notice and the return page already use;
          two literals here would be two chances for one to be corrected on its own.

          **The address is its own link text**, on both. Somebody reading this on a phone at
          the point of entry taps it, and somebody hearing it through a screen reader is read
          the address rather than the word "here". */
        }
        <li>
          Entries can be transferred up to <strong>{race.transferDeadline}</strong>,
          please contact us at{' '}
          <a href={`mailto:${race.contact}`}>{race.contact}</a> prior to the deadline to arrange
          the transfer.
        </li>
        <li>
          Refunds cannot be given, save for exceptional circumstances, at the Race
          Organiser's discretion. Please contact us at{' '}
          <a href={`mailto:${race.contact}`}>{race.contact}</a>.
        </li>
        {
          /* **"18 or over on race day" stays as prose, and it is a second statement of a rule
          the database enforces.** `entries.events.minimum_age` is 18 and
          `create_pending_purchase()` re-checks it on every submission, so this sentence cannot
          make an under-age entry possible — but it can go stale if the committee ever moves
          the age, and nothing would catch that. Wiring this page to the column would mean a
          database round trip on a static page and a Worker rewriting branch it does not
          otherwise need, which is a larger change than the fact is worth today. Recorded as a
          known duplication rather than left to be discovered. */
        }
        <li>Entrants must be 18 or over on race day.</li>
        <li>
          By taking part in this event, you confirm that your name and/or
          photographic/video footage taken during their participation may be used to
          publicise the Nightingale Nightmare and Southville Running Club, as well as for
          the fancy dress competition on the day. Tell us if you would rather not appear
          and we will not use one we know you are in.
        </li>
        <li>
          The Race Organisers reserve the right to refuse or cancel applications,
          including duplicate applications, or alter the date of the event, the course
          route or distance.
        </li>
        <li>
          The Race Organisers, marshals, sponsors, charities, suppliers and/or their
          agents will not be liable for any injury, loss or expense which may arise in
          consequence of your participation in this event, save as to negligence.
        </li>
        <li>
          Race marshals and medical team members have the authority to disqualify and
          remove any runner they consider to be acting dangerously, or to be unfit to
          compete.
        </li>
        <li>
          In the event of any dispute the decision of the Race Referee and Race Organisers
          shall be final.
        </li>
      </ul>

      <h2>Race Rules</h2>

      <ul>
        <li>
          Entrants are required to abide by these Event Terms &amp; Conditions, Race Rules
          and Marshals' directions.
        </li>
        {
          /* **The collection time and the race HQ both come from `race.json`.** `09:15` is the
          schedule's registration row — one value, read by name; `hqName` is the short form of
          `location`, which this sentence wants rather than the full postal address. */
        }
        <li>
          Race numbers will not be posted in advance of the event and shall be available
          for collection at the Race HQ at {race.hqName} from {registration.time} onwards on{
            ' '
          }{race.dateShort}.
        </li>
        <li>
          Runners must ensure that their race numbers are visible to ensure fair and
          accurate timing.
        </li>
        <li>Stay on the marked route, and take your litter with you.</li>
        <li>This event is not suitable for wheelchair athletes.</li>
        <li>
          In accordance with UKA Rule 240 the wearing of headphones or similar devices
          (other than those medically prescribed) is not permitted. The Race Organisers
          reserve the right to disqualify any competitor found in breach of this rule.
        </li>
        <li>Toilet facilities and limited changing will be available at the Race HQ.</li>
      </ul>

      <p>
        These Terms &amp; Conditions and Race Rules are subject to change by the Race
        Organisers.
      </p>

      {
        /* **The version line, and the date in it is load-bearing.** The document says in its
        own last sentence that it is subject to change, so somebody who entered on 1 September
        needs to be able to say which version they agreed to — and the club needs to be able to
        answer them. `entry_purchases.consents_version` records the wording a person ticked
        against; this is the human-readable half of the same fact.

        **It claims what is true and no more.** The race director supplied this copy; the
        committee has not ratified it. Writing "agreed by the committee" here would put a false
        statement of provenance on a legal document, which is the one thing worse than having
        no provenance line at all.

        **A plain `<p>`, with no class and no new CSS.** `/nn/privacy/` ends with
        "Last updated: …" the same way, which is the register this belongs in — and a long
        legal document is exactly what `.nn-prose` already expresses. */
      }
      <p>Version 1 — published 28 August 2026. Supplied by the race director.</p>
    </div>

    <footer>
      <p>
        <a href="/nn/2026/">Back to Nightingale Nightmare 2026</a>
      </p>
      <p>
        <a href="/nn/privacy/">What the club does with your details</a>
      </p>
    </footer>
  </div>

  {
    /* The same decorative artwork as every other page under /nn/, and empty for the same
    reason — it is a CSS background. See the artwork section of nn-theme.css. */
  }
  <div class="nn-hands" aria-hidden="true"></div>
</Base>
